  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Reductive ozonolysis of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math> followed by hydrolysis gives only one type of ketones because of symmetry across the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and bonding of two same alkyl groups <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced></math> with both the carbons bonded through double bond.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/4fb0fc37-4690-463f-88d9-65f335775666-530db92e-b486-4eb8-931c-0508e71f96c5-image.png\" style=\"width: 526px; height: 167px;\" /></p>",
